ext\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"regularly\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "In the past decade, family structures in many countries have changed profoundly. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Most adults have to be gainfully employed in order to make a living. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Expressing What is Necessary", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use certain expressions to talk about what is necessary to do in the future in order for something to happen.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<ul><li>You have to ... <li>You have got to \u2026 </li><li>I'm going to have to \u2026 </li><li>You need to \u2026</li>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "More and more people have to struggle endlessly in order to balance their work and family lives.   ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Most adults have to be gainfully employed in order to make a living. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "All of these members of the family are going to have be flexible to adapt to change.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "infant ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "baby ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Mothers of infants are more likely to return to work after a leave than before.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about families.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "toddler", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a young child who is just learning to walk", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Toddlers require a lot of attention and care.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": 