in a household where both parents work, or where the only parent works.", "id": 2, "time": "9100", "image": "engenn6le13ob09re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "Parents choose to work for different reasons. Challenging career opportunities have emerged. But, more importantly, in many families, both parents have to be gainfully employed in order to make a living. Mothers of infants and toddlers are more likely to return to work after a leave of absence than before. It is also more common to see grandparents raising their grandchildren. Personally, I think all family members are going to have to be flexible to adapt to change.", "id": 3, "time": "31500", "image": "engenn6le13ob09re2img03.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn6le13ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn6le13ob09re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": [], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1}]}]}